DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     ddmmeessgg displays the contents of the system message buffer.  It is most
     commonly used to review system startup messages.  On some systems the
     message buffer can survive reboot and be retained (in the hope of expos‐
     ing information from a crash).

     The options are as follows:

     --MM _c_o_r_e
             Extract values associated with the name list from the specified
             _c_o_r_e instead of the default _/_d_e_v_/_k_m_e_m.

     --NN _s_y_s_t_e_m
             Extract the name list from the specified _s_y_s_t_e_m instead of the
             default _/_b_s_d.

     --ss      Display the contents of the console message buffer instead.  This
             can be used to review rc(8) system startup messages.  This option
             is limited to the superuser.

FFIILLEESS
     /var/run/dmesg.boot  copy of ddmmeessgg saved by rc(8) at boot time

